# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
#  🎵  [general] — Core Visualizer Settings
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

[general]

    # ── Frequency Range ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # Human hearing: 20Hz - 20kHz
    # Sub-bass:  20  -  60 Hz  (rumble, kick drum body)
    # Bass:      60  - 250 Hz  (warmth, bass guitar)
    # Low-mid:  250  - 500 Hz  (muddiness zone)
    # Mid:      500  - 2kHz    (vocals, guitar, presence)
    # High-mid:   2k -   4kHz  (clarity, attack transients)
    # Presence:   4k -   6kHz  (consonants, definition)
    # Brilliance: 6k -  20kHz  (air, shimmer, cymbals)
    #
    # ASH recommended range: full spectrum with bass emphasis
    lower_cutoff_freq = 20
    upper_cutoff_freq = 20000

    # ── Bar Count ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # Higher = more frequency resolution, more beautiful
    # Recommended: 50-200 depending on terminal width
    # For shader output: 200 (shader handles rendering)
    # For terminal output: auto (fits terminal width)
    bars = 200

    # ── Frame Rate ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # Target frames per second for visualization
    # 60 = butter-smooth, matches most display refresh rates
    # Higher values increase CPU usage proportionally
    # Range: 1 - 200
    framerate = 60

    # ── Sensitivity ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # Auto-sensitivity adjusts gain based on input level
    # 1 = on (recommended — adapts to music volume automatically)
    # 0 = off (use manual gain below)
    autosens = 1

    # Manual sensitivity (only if autosens = 0)
    # Range: 1 - 1000 (100 = neutral, higher = more amplification)
    sensitivity = 100

    # ── Averaging ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # Average bars (smooths out impulse spikes across neighbors)
    # 0 = no averaging
    # 1 = average with immediate neighbors
    # 2 = wider averaging
    # ASH: 0 for maximum responsiveness with shader gravity
    overshoot = 20

    # ── Channels ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # stereo = split left/right (beautiful mirror effect)
    # mono   = combined channel (simpler, wider bars)
    # left   = left channel only
    # right  = right channel only
    channels = stereo

    # ── Stereo Arrangement ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # When channels = stereo, how to arrange L/R
    # normal    = L on left, R on right (natural)
    # mirror    = both expand from center (explosion effect — BEST for ASH)
    # combine   = channels overlap in one display
    stereo_arrangement = mirror

    # ── Mode ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # normal = standard frequency bars
    # parabola = parabolic interpolation (smoother curves)
    mode = normal

    # ── Frequency Weighting ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # none     = flat (shows raw FFT data)
    # A        = A-weighting (human hearing sensitivity — RECOMMENDED)
    # B        = B-weighting
    # C        = C-weighting
    # D        = D-weighting
    # Musical  = emphasis on musical content
    # Mel      = mel scale (perceptual pitch)
    frequency_scale = log

    # ── Waveform ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # If > 0, shows raw waveform instead of spectrum
    # Useful for oscilloscope-style visualization
    waveform = 0

    # ── Zero Test ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # Test if source outputs zeros (silence detection)
    zero_test = 0

    # ── Noise Reduction ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # 0.0 = no noise reduction (maximum detail)
    # 0.77 = default noise gate
    # 1.0 = maximum noise reduction
    noise_reduction = 0.77

# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
#  🔊  [input] — Audio Source Configuration
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

[input]

    # ── Audio Method ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # auto        = auto-detect best available (recommended)
    # pipewire    = PipeWire (modern Wayland audio — PREFERRED)
    # pulse       = PulseAudio
    # alsa        = ALSA direct
    # fifo        = read from named pipe (MPD integration)
    # sndio       = sndio (OpenBSD/FreeBSD)
    # oss         = OSS (legacy)
    # jack        = JACK audio
    # portaudio   = PortAudio cross-platform
    method = pipewire

    # ── Audio Source ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # auto         = default sink monitor (capture system audio output)
    # /dev/dsp     = OSS device
    # hw:0,0       = ALSA hardware device
    # default      = PulseAudio default monitor
    # For PipeWire: use monitor source (captures all playback)
    source = auto

    # ── Sample Rate ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # Sample rate in Hz — must match your audio interface
    # 44100 = CD quality (most common)
    # 48000 = professional/studio (PipeWire default)
    # 96000 = high-definition
    sample_rate = 44100

    # ── Sample Size ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # Bits per sample
    # 16 = standard quality
    # 32 = high precision (more accurate FFT)
    sample_size = 16

    # ── Channels ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # Number of input channels to read (1=mono, 2=stereo)
    channels = 2

    # ── FIFO Path ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # Used when method = fifo (e.g., MPD visualization)
    # Configure MPD to output to this pipe:
    #   audio_output { type "fifo" path "/tmp/mpd.fifo" format "44100:16:2" }
    # source = /tmp/mpd.fifo

# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
#  🖥️  [output] — Display / Rendering Configuration
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

[output]

    # ── Output Method ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # ncurses    = terminal rendering (classic, most compatible)
    # noncurses  = terminal without ncurses (faster in some cases)
    # raw        = raw data output (for pipe to other programs)
    # nyan       = nyan-cat style rainbow (fun!)
    # opengl     = OpenGL rendering (GLSL shaders — PREMIUM ASH MODE)
    # sdl2       = SDL2 window rendering
    # sdl2_gles  = SDL2 with OpenGL ES
    #
    # ASH ULTRA: use opengl for GLSL shader support
    # Fallback to ncurses if OpenGL not available
    method = opengl

    # ── Raw Output Format ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # Used when method = raw
    # bit_format: 8bit | 16bit
    # data_format: binary | ascii
    # ascii_delimiters: characters between bars (e.g. "\n", ";")
    bit_format = 16bit
    data_format = binary
    ascii_max_range = 1000
    ascii_delimiters = "\n"

    # ── Bar Orientation ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # bottom = bars grow upward from bottom (classic)
    # top    = bars grow downward from top
    # left   = bars grow rightward from left (sideways)
    # right  = bars grow leftward from right (sideways)
    orientation = bottom

    # ── Bar Style (ncurses/noncurses) ────────────────────────────────────────
    # unicode_block = filled block characters (▁▂▃▄▅▆▇█)
    # half_block    = finer resolution with half blocks
    # braille       = braille dots for ultra-fine resolution
    # Determines look in terminal mode (shader overrides in opengl mode)
    bar_style = braille

    # ── Bar Width & Spacing ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # bar_width: characters per bar (terminal mode)
    # bar_spacing: characters between bars
    # Ignored in OpenGL mode (shader controls geometry)
    bar_width = 2
    bar_spacing = 1

    # ── Bar Delimiter ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # Character at the very bottom of each bar (visual anchor)
    # '' = no delimiter, '─' = line, '═' = double line
    bar_delimiter = 0

    # ── Bit Resolution (terminal) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
    # 8  = 256 height levels
    # 16 = 65536 height levels (sub-character precision)
    bit_format = 16bit

    # ── OpenGL / SDL Window Settings ─────────────────────────────────────────
    # Window dimensions for standalone OpenGL/SDL rendering
    # Ignored when embedded in terminal (Kitty, etc.)
    opengl_width = 1920
    opengl_height = 200

    # ── GLSL Shader ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # Path to fragment shader (absolute or relative to this config)
    # ASH ships with two premium shaders:
    #   bar_spectrum.frag    — classic spectrum bars with glow effects
    #   northern_lights.frag — flowing aurora-style visualization
    #
    # Switch shaders via ASH: ash theme apply <name>
    # Or manually edit this line and restart cava
    opengl_shader = ~/.config/cava/shaders/bar_spectrum.frag

    # ── Terminal Color Support ────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # Fallback for ncurses mode (when OpenGL unavailable)
    # 16   = standard 16 terminal colors
    # 256  = 256-color palette
    # 16M  = true 24-bit color (requires: export COLORTERM=truecolor)
    terminal_color_type = 16M

    # ── Foreground / Background Colors (ncurses fallback) ────────────────────
    # Format: 'COLOR;COLOR;COLOR' (gradient stops, 1-8 values)
    # Colors: black, red, green, yellow, blue, magenta, cyan, white
    #       or hex: '#rrggbb' (requires terminal_color_type = 16M)
    #
    # ASH Dynamic: these are overwritten by ash theme engine
    # Default: Catppuccin Mocha Mauve → Blue → Teal gradient
    foreground = '#cba6f7;#89b4fa;#74c7ec;#94e2d5;#a6e3a1'
    background = '#1e1e2e'

    # ── Gradient ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # Enable gradient coloring of bars (bottom to top)
    # 0 = solid color
    # 1 = gradient (uses gradient_color_1 through gradient_color_8)
    gradient = 1

    # Gradient color stops (bottom → top of bar)
    # ASH Dark theme: Deep blue → Mauve → Pink (depth to highlight)
    gradient_count = 8
    gradient_color_1 = '#313244'
    gradient_color_2 = '#585b70'
    gradient_color_3 = '#7f849c'
    gradient_color_4 = '#89b4fa'
    gradient_color_5 = '#b4befe'
    gradient_color_6 = '#cba6f7'
    gradient_color_7 = '#f5c2e7'
    gradient_color_8 = '#f38ba8'

    # ── Overlay / Mono Color Mode ─────────────────────────────────────────────
    # mono = single color for all bars (simpler but faster)
    # Colors for mono mode:
    # mono_color = '#cba6f7'

    # ── Sine Mode ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # Draws a smooth sine curve through bar tops
    # (visual only, doesn't affect audio analysis)
    # 0 = off, 1 = on
    # Incompatible with braille bar_style
    # sine = 0

    # ── Opacity ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # Bar opacity for opengl mode (0.0 = invisible, 1.0 = fully opaque)
    # Allows background content to show through (e.g. wallpaper)
    opacity = 1.0

# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
#  🎛️  [smoothing] — Animation & Motion Quality
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

[smoothing]

    # ── Integral Smoothing ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # Temporal smoothing: mixes current frame with previous frames
    # Higher = smoother transitions, more "inertia" feel
    # 0 = no smoothing (instant response, jittery)
    # 77 = default (good balance)
    # 90+ = very smooth, dreamy / slow response
    # Range: 0 - 100
    integral = 77

    # ── Gravity ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # How fast bars fall after a peak (like gravity pulling them down)
    # Lower = bars fall faster (snappy)
    # Higher = bars float down slowly (liquid/heavy feel)
    # 0 = instant drop (no gravity)
    # Range: 0 - 100
    # ASH: 75 = satisfying heavy-liquid drop
    gravity = 75

    # ── Overshoot ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # Allow bars to briefly exceed actual level (spring physics)
    # Creates a "bounce" effect on transients
    # 0 = no overshoot (precise)
    # Higher = more spring/bounce
    # Range: 0 - 200
    # ASH: 20 = subtle natural spring
    overshoot = 20

    # ── Waves ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # Add a wave effect across all bars (undulating motion)
    # 0 = no wave (clean bars)
    # 1+ = wave amplitude
    # ASH: 0 = clean, let shader handle wave effects
    waves = 0

    # ── Equalizer ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # Per-bar frequency equalizer for visual balance
    # Format: "bar_num:multiplier bar_num:multiplier ..."
    # Boost bass bars slightly for visual impact
    # equalizer = "1:1.5 2:1.4 3:1.3 4:1.2 5:1.1"

    # ── Gravity Direction ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # Which direction bars fall after peaks
    # down = fall toward bottom (standard)
    # up   = fall toward top (inverted)
    gravity_direction = down

# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
#  🎹  [eq] — Frequency Equalizer (Visual Balance)
#
#  Fine-tune visual amplitudes per frequency range.
#  Human perception: bass feels louder than treble at same dB.
#  These values compensate for perceptual imbalance.
#
#  Bar mapping (200 bars, 20Hz - 20kHz log scale):
#  Bars 1-20    ≈ 20Hz  -  80Hz   (sub-bass)
#  Bars 21-50   ≈ 80Hz  - 250Hz   (bass)
#  Bars 51-100  ≈ 250Hz -  1kHz   (low-mid)
#  Bars 101-140 ≈ 1kHz  -  4kHz   (mid/high-mid)
#  Bars 141-180 ≈ 4kHz  -  10kHz  (presence)
#  Bars 181-200 ≈ 10kHz -  20kHz  (air/brilliance)
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

[eq]

    # Sub-bass boost (kick drum, bass rumble — visually impactful)
    1 = 1.8
    2 = 1.7
    3 = 1.6
    4 = 1.5
    5 = 1.45

    # Bass (warmth, bass guitar)
    6 = 1.4
    7 = 1.35
    8 = 1.30
    9 = 1.25
    10 = 1.20

    # Low-mid transition
    11 = 1.15
    12 = 1.10
    13 = 1.05
    14 = 1.00
    15 = 0.95

    # Mid (neutral — vocals sit here)
    16 = 0.95
    17 = 0.95
    18 = 0.95
    19 = 0.95
    20 = 0.95

    # Upper-mid (presence, attack)
    21 = 0.90
    22 = 0.90
    23 = 0.90
    24 = 0.90
    25 = 0.90

    # High-mid to high (gradual roll-off for balance)
    26 = 0.85
    27 = 0.85
    28 = 0.85
    29 = 0.85
    30 = 0.85

    # Presence (slight boost for visual excitement)
    31 = 0.90
    32 = 0.90
    33 = 0.90
    34 = 0.90
    35 = 0.90

    # Brilliance / air (boost high end — visually exciting)
    36 = 1.00
    37 = 1.05
    38 = 1.10
    39 = 1.15
    40 = 1.20

# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
#  🎨  ASH THEME INTEGRATION
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
#
#  ASH Theme Engine automatically updates:
#  ┌─────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────┐
#  │ Config Key                  │ Source                                   │
#  ├─────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────┤
#  │ foreground                  │ theme accent color gradient              │
#  │ background                  │ theme base color                         │
#  │ gradient_color_1..8         │ theme color spectrum (8 stops)           │
#  │ opengl_shader               │ selected shader mode                     │
#  └─────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────┘
#
#  Theme gradient presets by category:
#  ┌──────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
#  │ Theme                │ Gradient Style                               │
#  ├──────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
#  │ catppuccin-mocha     │ Surface → Blue → Mauve → Pink               │
#  │ tokyo-night          │ Dark → Cyan → Blue → Purple                 │
#  │ gruvbox-dark         │ Dark → Orange → Yellow → Green              │
#  │ nord                 │ Dark → Frost blue → Polar night             │
#  │ dracula              │ Dark → Purple → Pink → Red                  │
#  │ rose-pine            │ Dark → Pine → Rose → Gold                   │
#  │ cyberpunk-2077       │ Black → Cyan → Yellow → White               │
#  │ synthwave-84         │ Dark → Purple → Pink → Hot pink             │
#  │ matrix               │ Black → Dark green → Bright green           │
#  │ aurora-borealis      │ Dark → Teal → Green → Magenta              │
#  │ vaporwave            │ Dark → Pink → Purple → Cyan                 │
#  └──────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
#
#  Reload after theme change: pkill -USR1 cava
#  Or via ASH:               ash theme apply <name>
#
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
#
#  Keyboard shortcuts (while cava is running):
#  ┌─────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────┐
#  │ Key     │ Action                                   │
#  ├─────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────┤
#  │ q / ESC │ Quit                                     │
#  │ r       │ Reload config (hot-reload)               │
#  │ c       │ Cycle through gradient colors            │
